# Sakura PC — core workflow (always follow)

This rule applies to **every** agent turn in this repo. It complements the other `.cursor/rules/*` files (Supabase, Solana, media, etc.); when in conflict on **build or Electron delivery**, this rule wins.

## What this project is

- **Next.js** (App Router, static export where applicable) + **React** client UI.
- **Electron** desktop shell (`electron/main.js`, `electron/preload.js`); production loads the built web app (`app://` or file protocol per existing setup).
- **HiAnime backend** bundled as `hianime-node` (port **4789**); the renderer talks to it via `NEXT_PUBLIC_CONSUMET_URL` (typically `http://localhost:4789` at build time for Electron).
- **Capacitor** types/plugins** appear in shared code; treat **Electron + web** as first-class; do not break Android/iOS paths without an explicit request.

## Agent behavior (non-negotiable)

- **Execute** build and copy steps yourself when the user asks for a desktop build or “send to desktop” — do not only paste instructions.
- Prefer **PowerShell-safe** commands on Windows: use `;` instead of `&&` when chaining in PowerShell, or run separate invocations.
- Keep changes **minimal and task-scoped**; do not refactor unrelated modules or add docs the user did not ask for.
- After substantive app changes that affect the packaged app, assume a **full desktop build + copy to Desktop** is expected unless the user explicitly opts out.

## Build — when to run

Run a full pipeline when:

- The user asks to **build**, **package**, **electron build**, **release**, or **copy to desktop**; or
- You changed **Electron** (`electron/**`), **`hianime-node/**`**, **Next config**, **env vars baked into the client**, or anything that affects the **packaged** `.exe` / `win-unpacked` output.

## Build — standard sequence (Windows)

From the repo root (path contains `sakura-pc`):

1. **Optional clean** (recommended after dependency or Next config changes):

   `if (Test-Path .next) { Remove-Item -Recurse -Force .next }`

2. **Next.js production build** (required before Electron pack):

   `npx next build`

3. **Electron / Windows artifact** (uses `electron-builder` per `package.json`):

   `npx electron-builder --win`

   Use the same **`NEXT_PUBLIC_CONSUMET_URL`** strategy as in `package.json` (`electron:build` uses `http://localhost:4789`) so the packaged app matches production expectations.

4. **Verify output** under `dist-electron\` (e.g. `win-unpacked\`, installer if configured).

If a step fails, **fix or report** the error; do not declare success without a clean exit code.

## Copy to Desktop — standard sequence

After a successful `electron-builder` run:

1. **Stop a running Sakura instance** so files are not locked:

   `Stop-Process -Name "Sakura" -ErrorAction SilentlyContinue`

   Then short sleep (e.g. 2 seconds) before copying.

2. **Deploy folder copy** — replace the previous Desktop copy with the new `win-unpacked`:

   - Remove old folder if present:
     `if (Test-Path "$env:USERPROFILE\Desktop\Sakura") { Remove-Item -Recurse -Force "$env:USERPROFILE\Desktop\Sakura" }`
   - Copy fresh build:
     `Copy-Item -Recurse -Force "dist-electron\win-unpacked" "$env:USERPROFILE\Desktop\Sakura"`

Use **`$env:USERPROFILE\Desktop\Sakura`** so the rule works for any Windows user; only use a hard-coded path if the user explicitly requires it.

## Do not

- Skip the **Next** build before **electron-builder** when producing a new desktop bundle.
- Copy **only** `out/` without running **electron-builder** when the user asked for the **desktop app**.
- Introduce secrets into committed files; keep tokens in env or user-level config.

## Quick reference

| Goal | Commands |
|------|----------|
| Web-only production | `npx next build` |
| Desktop bundle | clean `.next` (optional) → `npx next build` → `npx electron-builder --win` |
| Desktop folder for testing | copy `dist-electron\win-unpacked` → `%USERPROFILE%\Desktop\Sakura` |
